// Five bodies at exactly the same point — the case that produces NaN, driven
// through the whole simulation rather than one unit test. See `crate::contact`
// for why a coincident pair has no line to push along, and the runner's
// `check_finite` for why a poisoned position passes ordinary assertions.
//
// It is not contrived: a crowd converging on one target arrives at one point,
// which is what seeking produces.
//
// Measured: the cluster settles on tick 15, and the golden trace records the
// whole descent — ten pairs, then five, then four while the line straightens,
// then nothing. The budget is 60 so "and stays settled" is part of the file.
//
// The tolerances below are **bounds, not precisions** — the deliberate
// exception to the rule that a wide tolerance is an assertion switched off.
// What they assert is that the cluster did not detonate.
(
    description: "Five bodies at one point fan out to a stable ring instead of NaN.",
    setup: (
        actions: [
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
            Place((20.0, 0.0)),
        ],
    ),
    inputs: [],
    budget: (ticks: 60),
    expect: (
        contacts: 0,
        crowd_contacts: 0,
        enemy_count: 5,
        bodies: [
            (nth: 0, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
            (nth: 1, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
            (nth: 2, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
            (nth: 3, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
            (nth: 4, alive: true, pos: (x: 20.0, z: 0.0, tol: 1.5)),
        ],
        trace: "a_coincident_cluster_fans_out.trace",
    ),
)
